# Product AI feature paths where assistant and model-provider names (class B
# terms) are allowed because they are features of Orcon itself (SPEC-006).
# AI authorship marks (class A) stay forbidden here too.
# One glob per line, each with a reason: "glob  # reason". Add a glob only in a
# reviewed pull request, and only for a product AI feature (tooling.md TOOL-4.5).

internal/ai/**  # AI agents and provider-facing logic (SPEC-006)
internal/adapter/llm/**  # model provider adapters (SPEC-006)
internal/adapter/mcpserver/**  # MCP server exposed to AI clients (ADR-0059)
internal/adapter/mcpclient/**  # MCP client used by AI agents (ADR-0067)
internal/n8nimport/**  # mapping of n8n AI nodes (ADR-0071)
internal/adapter/codec/n8n/**  # n8n export format with its AI node types (SPEC-006 21.3)
internal/retrieval/**  # knowledge ingestion and embedding providers (ADR-0065)
docs/adr/006[0-9]-*.md  # AI ADRs 0060-0069 (SPEC-006)
docs/adr/007[0-2]-*.md  # AI ADRs 0070-0072 (SPEC-006)
packages/openapi/v1/**  # provider enumerations in the API contract
docs/reference/n8n-ai-coverage.md  # n8n AI node coverage table (SPEC-006 21.3)
docs/reference/ai-prices*  # model price tables by provider (SPEC-006 21.3)
docs/reference/connectors/ai/**  # reference pages of AI connectors
test/mockllm/**  # mock model provider used by tests (SPEC-006 21.3)
docs/design-system/mockups/ux-2026-10/index.html  # approved UX mockup: the model-provider credential and AI step of the product (SPEC-006, SPEC-019)
docs/design-system/mockups/ux-2026-10/DECISIONS.md  # design decisions of the same mockup: the model-provider credential example (SPEC-019)
cmd/orcon/wire_agent.go  # wiring of the model provider adapters of the agent node (SPEC-006)
cmd/orcon/whatsapp_agent_e2e_test.go  # end-to-end test of the agent flow with a scripted model (SPEC-006)
examples/flows/whatsapp-agent.json  # example flow whose model node names its provider (SPEC-006)

# Not a product AI feature: the only non-product entry. This file holds the
# line-ending block that mneme writes for the tool configuration directories,
# which has to name them. It is flagged for the owner's confirmation.
.gitattributes  # mneme-managed block naming the tool configuration directories
